{
  "an10.176:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.176 ",
  "an10.176:0.2": "17. With Jānussoṇi ",
  "an10.176:0.3": "With Cunda ",
  "an10.176:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an10.176:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Pāvā in Cunda the smith’s mango grove. ",
  "an10.176:1.3": "Then Cunda the smith went to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. The Buddha said to him, ",
  "an10.176:1.4": "“Cunda, whose purity do you believe in?” ",
  "an10.176:1.5": "“Sir, I believe in the purity advocated by the western brahmins garlanded with aquatic flowers who carry pitchers, serve the sacred flame, and immerse themselves in water.” ",
  "an10.176:2.1": "“But Cunda, what kind of purity do these western brahmins advocate?” ",
  "an10.176:2.2": "“The western brahmins encourage their disciple like this: ",
  "an10.176:2.3": "‘Please, my man, rising early you should stroke the earth from your bed. ",
  "an10.176:2.4": "If you don’t stroke the earth, stroke fresh cow dung. ",
  "an10.176:2.5": "If you don’t stroke fresh cow dung, stroke green grass. ",
  "an10.176:2.6": "If you don’t stroke green grass, serve the sacred flame. ",
  "an10.176:2.7": "If you don’t serve the sacred flame, revere the sun with cupped palms. ",
  "an10.176:2.8": "If you don’t revere the sun with cupped palms, immerse yourself in water three times, including at dusk.’ ",
  "an10.176:2.9": "The western brahmins advocate this kind of purity.” ",
  "an10.176:3.1": "“The purity advocated by the western brah